<title>GERMANY: D.Telekom plans to reduce debt 12 bln DM.</title>
<headline>D.Telekom plans to reduce debt 12 bln DM.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German telecommunications giant Deutsche Telekom AG plans to reduce its debt by 12 billion marks this year, which would save interest payments in the hundreds of millions of marks, chief finance officer Joachim Kroeske said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
